The treatment was carried out between and, with the following characteristics:
- device: linear accelerator Clinic;
- energy of the accelerated electrons: MeV; 
- number of fractions and dose per session: 25 sessions at 50 Gray;
- conformal three-dimensional radiotherapy for the entire chest wall, with modulation of the intensity of the beam, which took into account the variability of the thickness of the tissue traversed by the rays (density);
- external radiation to the right supraclavicular region (crenshaw area):
- 46 Gray in 23 equal portions spread over five weeks;
- internal mammary chain irradiated with four internal fields on both sides:
- 46 Gray in 23 equal portions spread over five weeks;
- right lung volume dose calculation according to the Lyman system:
- V20: 17.81%;
- V30: 15.89%;
- heart dose: mean dose 2.38 Gy (maximum constraint dose 4 Gy).
In conclusion, my opinion is that this case study presents a good practice example of reporting a breast radiotherapy case report, taking into account all the requirements set out in the call for tenders. I hope you will find it useful. If you have any further questions or need more clarifications, please do not hesitate to write me back. Wish you good health.assistantHello! Welcome and thank you for asking on this medical LLM.! Regarding your concern, I would explain that the provided information seems to be incomplete (no information are available concerning chemotherapy and hormonal therapy). Anyway, considering the total amount of dose delivered during this course of radiotherapy, it can be considered as adequate. The main finding in this case, which could lead to a moderate increase of the risk for chronic side effects related to radiotherapy (fibrosis, etc.), is the high dose received by the lungs. Another important aspect, considering her age, is the possible cardiac exposure (the heart volume is inside the field of radiation). For this reason, periodic monitoring of cardiac function may be necessary. Hope you will find this answer helpful! Kind regards,

